error[E0277]: `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>` has no storage of its own type, so a parameter cannot borrow one
 --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_result.rs:8:1
  |
8 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this parameter is taken by reference
  |
  = help: the trait `Borrowable<__R>` is not implemented for `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>`
  = note: a borrowed aggregate crosses as its projection: where `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>` is a `#[derive(TyArg)] #[projection]` aggregate, write `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>Ref<'_>`, or `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>Mut<'_>` for a struct and `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>Mut<'_, Rt>` for an enum (RFC-0050 rule 6).
  = note: an Option has no storage of its own type to borrow: `None` is one value and `Some(v)` is `v`'s own value, so nothing behind a reference is shaped like an `Option<T>`. Take `Option<&T>`, or the option by value.
  = note: a Rust slice is not one of the language's types: take `Slice<T, Rt>`, the language's `&[T]` (RFC-0047).
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Borrowable<Rt>`:
            `()` implements `Borrowable<__Rt>`
            `Arr<T, N>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `Erased<R, T>` implements `Borrowable<R>`
            `Spec<T>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `Typeck<N>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `Vec<T>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `acvus_extern::Owned<R>` implements `Borrowable<R>`
            `bool` implements `Borrowable<__Rt>`
          and $N others
  = note: required for `ByRef<std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>>` to implement `for<'a> Arg<'a, __R>`
  = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `extern_fn` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

error[E0277]: `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>` has no storage of its own type at a monomorphized member, so a parameter cannot borrow one
  --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_result.rs:13:1
   |
13 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this parameter of a monomorphized member is taken by reference
   |
   = help: the trait `BorrowableSpecialized<__R>` is not implemented for `std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>`
   = note: a Result crosses a member by value: a crossed `Result` is the language's flat variant, not Rust's `Result<Owned, Owned>`, so nothing behind a reference is shaped like a `Result<T, E>` (RFC-0050 rule 8).
   = note: an Option crosses a member by value: `None` is one value and `Some(v)` is `v`'s own value, so nothing behind a reference is shaped like an `Option<T>`. Take `Option<&T>` (RFC-0039).
   = help: the following other types implement trait `BorrowableSpecialized<Rt>`:
             `()` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
             `Vec<T>` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<Rt>`
             `bool` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
             `char` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
             `f64` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
             `i16` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
             `i32` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
             `i64` implements `BorrowableSpecialized<__Rt>`
           and $N others
   = note: required for `ByRef<std::result::Result<i64, std::string::String>, acvus_extern::Specialized>` to implement `for<'a> Arg<'a, __R>`
